package openrouter

const warmingInstructions = `You triage a slow GPU warming alert for a hardware team. Decide NOTIFY now if the observed thermal behavior warrants hardware investigation, or WATCH and reassess in a minute. Weigh persistent or increasing heat against pre-event operating temperatures and changes in power and utilization. A utilization signal may be unavailable. Do not claim a physical diagnosis. No future observations are supplied. Choose WATCH or NOTIFY. Times are seconds relative to the original alert. Rows are [time, Celsius, watts, percent utilization]; null means unavailable. Also use the supplied chronological plateau summaries. Each gives the first and last observed second and median values in the order of its named signals. Joint power/utilization plateaus require a 60s span within 25W and 5 percentage points; power-only plateaus cannot establish utilization; temperature plateaus require 45s within 1C. Missing samples can split a plateau. Compare the initial thermal response to a load step with subsequent temperature levels while that same load persists. A sustained second rise above a previously established loaded thermal plateau without another load increase warrants hardware investigation, even if temperature later levels off. A return to temperatures already seen under comparable load provides evidence for watching. `
